  "body": "## What this is\n\nPart 3 of a 3-PR stack fixing #128972. Stacks on #131493 (merge #131492 and #131493 first). This closes out the remaining sites of the same bug class, found during the audit for the main issue — not required to close #128972 itself, but the same root cause in a handful of other components.\n\n## Root cause\n\nA handful of raw anchors render a route path straight into `href` without applying `appSubUrl`:\n\n- `DataSourceCategories.tsx` — \"Find more data source plugins\" (also had `target=\"_self\"`, which made it skip `interceptLinkClicks`'s SPA rescue entirely — even a plain left-click did a real browser navigation to a 404 under a subpath)\n- `BuildDashboardButton.tsx` — the \"Build a dashboard\" `LinkButton` and its \"Blank\" `Menu.Item` (the url was also missing a leading slash, which is wrong even without a subpath)\n- `NewDataSource.tsx` — the Cancel button\n- `DataSourcesList.tsx` — the empty-state \"Add data source\" button\n- `AdvisorRedirectNotice.tsx` — the \"Go to Advisor\" link\n\nNone of these double the subpath (that's PRs 1–2); these drop it, so they only break on cmd+click, open-in-new-tab, and copy-link (a plain left-click is rescued by `interceptLinkClicks`, except the `DataSourceCategories` case above).\n\n## Fix\n\nApply `locationUtil.assureBaseUrl` at each site, matching the existing convention already used in `DataSourcesListCard.tsx` / `AddNewDataSourceButton.tsx`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- New `DataSourceCategories.test.tsx` covering the \"Find more data source plugins\" href under a subpath.\n- New `PageCard.test.tsx` — a regression guard for `PageCard`, which already renders correctly via a raw `href` (fixed by #130603) but had no test locking that in.\n- `BuildDashboardButton.test.tsx` / `EditDataSourceActions.test.tsx` updated for the added leading slash.\n\n```\nyarn jest --no-watch --watchAll=false public/app/features/connections public/app/features/datasources/components\nyarn tsc --noEmit\n```",
